          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='9171' id='12' type-v2='text' w='98720' x='640' y='89996'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='10'><![CDATA[Blue bars show flight volume, cause share, or median delay severity depending on the chart; orange lines show departure delay rate. Each departure-delayed flight is assigned the cause with the largest positive cause-specific delay minutes; flights without positive cause-specific minutes are labeled "No Reported Cause." NAS means National Airspace System delays, such as airport operations, heavy traffic volume, air traffic control, or other non-extreme-weather system constraints. Distance groups are Short (<500 miles), Medium (500-999), Long (1,000-1,999), and Very Long (2,000+). Severity values are medians among flights departing at least 15 minutes late.]]></run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
